sage data via read(0,buf,size), stores pointer in msg[cookie_num] and size in msg_size[cookie_num], increments cookie_num.\"},{\"name\":\"eat_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x14e1\",\"callers\":[\"main\"],\"callees\":[\"_abort\",\"fread\",\"printf\",\"free\",\"__stack_chk_fail\"],\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"random_byte\",\"source\":\"fread from /dev/urandom\",\"type\":\"char\",\"stack\":\"rbp-0xc\"}],\"checks\":[\"if cookie_num == 0 → _abort('No cookie!')\"],\"memory_operations\":[{\"operation\":\"READ\",\"source\":\"fread(&random_byte, 1, 1, urandom)\"},{\"operation\":\"COMPUTE\",\"description\":\"index = random_byte % cookie_num (signed idiv)\"},{\"operation\":\"READ\",\"source\":\"msg[index]\",\"address\":\"0x4060 + index*8\",\"destination\":\"printf argument\"},{\"operation\":\"FREE\",\"target\":\"msg[index]\",\"note\":\"free(msg[index]) — pointer NOT nulled after free\"},{\"operation\":\"READ\",\"source\":\"msg[cookie_num-1]\",\"address\":\"0x4060 + (cookie_num-1)*8\"},{\"operation\":\"WRITE\",\"destination\":\"msg[index] = msg[cookie_num-1]\",\"address\":\"0x4060 + index*8\",\"note\":\"swap-remove: last element moved to freed slot\"},{\"operation\":\"READ\",\"source\":\"msg_size[cookie_num-1]\",\"address\":\"0x4160 + (cookie_num-1)*4\"},{\"operation\":\"WRITE\",\"destination\":\"msg_size[index] = msg_size[cookie_num-1]\",\"address\":\"0x4160 + index*4\"},{\"operation\":\"WRITE\",\"destination\":\"cookie_num -= 1\",\"address\":\"0x41e8\"}],\"calls\":[\"fread\",\"printf\",\"free\",\"_abort\"],\"summary\":\"Eats (deletes) a random cookie: reads 1 byte from /dev/urandom, computes index = byte % cookie_num, prints msg[index] via printf(%s), frees msg[index], then swap-removes by moving msg[cookie_num-1] into msg[index] and msg_size[cookie_num-1] into msg_size[index], decrements cookie_num. The freed pointer is NOT explicitly nulled — if index == cookie_num-1, the swap writes the same freed pointer back into msg[index].\"},{\"name\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1628\",\"callers\":[\"main\"],\"callees\":[\"printf\",\"__isoc99_scanf\",\"_abort\",\"read\",\"puts\",\"__stack_chk_fail\"],\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"index\",\"source\":\"scanf(%llu)\",\"type\":\"uint64\",\"stack\":\"rbp-0x10\"},{\"name\":\"edit_data\",\"source\":\"read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1)\",\"type\":\"raw bytes\"}],\"checks\":[\"index < cookie_num (cmp rdx,rax; jl — signed less-than comparison, but index read as unsigned %llu)\"],\"memory_operations\":[{\"operation\":\"READ\",\"source\":\"msg_size[index]\",\"address\":\"0x4160 + index*4\",\"destination\":\"read size = msg_size[index] - 1\"},{\"operation\":\"READ\",\"source\":\"msg[index]\",\"address\":\"0x4060 + index*8\",\"destination\":\"read buffer pointer\"},{\"operation\":\"WRITE\",\"destination\":\"msg[index] buffer\",\"size\":\"msg_size[index] - 1 (computed as int32, sign-extended via movsxd)\",\"source\":\"read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1)\"},{\"operation\":\"WRITE\",\"destination\":\"msg[index][read_return_value] = 0x00 if last byte == 0x0a\",\"note\":\"newline replacement\"}],\"calls\":[\"printf\",\"__isoc99_scanf\",\"read\",\"puts\",\"_abort\"],\"summary\":\"Edits a cookie message: reads index via scanf(%llu), checks index < cookie_num (signed jl), then reads msg_size[index]-1 bytes into msg[index] buffer via read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1). The size is computed as msg_size[index] (int32) - 1, sign-extended to int64 via movsxd. If msg_size[index] is 0, the subtraction yields -1 which sign-extends to 0xFFFFFFFF, causing read to attempt a massive write.\"},{\"name\":\"read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1751\",\"callers\":[\"main\"],\"callees\":[\"printf\",\"__isoc99_scanf\",\"_abort\",\"__stack_chk_fail\"],\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"index\",\"source\":\"scanf(%llu)\",\"type\":\"uint64\",\"stack\":\"rbp-0x10\"}],\"checks\":[\"index < cookie_num (cmp rdx,rax; jl — signed less-than comparison, but index read as unsigned %llu)\"],\"memory_operations\":[{\"operation\":\"READ\",\"source\":\"msg[index]\",\"address\":\"0x4060 + index*8\",\"destination\":\"printf(%s) argument\"}],\"calls\":[\"printf\",\"__isoc99_scanf\",\"_abort\"],\"summary\":\"Views a cookie message: reads index via scanf(%llu), checks index < cookie_num (signed jl), then prints msg[index] as a string via printf('%s', msg[index]).\"},{\"name\":\"menu\",\"address\":\"0x17fd\",\"callers\":[\"main\"],\"callees\":[\"puts\",\"__stack_chk_fail\"],\"inputs\":[],\"checks\":[],\"memory_operations\":[],\"calls\":[\"puts\"],\"summary\":\"Prints the menu options via puts.\"},{\"name\":\"main\",\"address\":\"0x187f\",\"callers\":[\"__libc_start_main\"],\"callees\":[\"init\",\"menu\",\"__isoc99_scanf\",\"eat_cookie\",\"create_cookie\",\"edit_cookie\",\"read_cookie\",\"exit\"],\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"choice\",\"source\":\"scanf(%lld)\",\"type\":\"int64\",\"stack\":\"rbp-0x10\"}],\"checks\":[\"choice == 1 → eat_cookie\",\"choice == 2 → create_cookie\",\"choice == 3 → edit_cookie\",\"choice == 4 → read_cookie\",\"choice == 5 → exit(0)\"],\"memory_operations\":[],\"calls\":[\"init\",\"menu\",\"__isoc99_scanf\",\"eat_cookie\",\"create_cookie\",\"edit_cookie\",\"read_cookie\",\"exit\"],\"summary\":\"Main loop: calls init(), then loops: print menu, scanf(%lld) choice, dispatch to eat/create/edit/read/exit.\"}],\"attack_surfaces\":[{\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"input\":\"random_byte from /dev/urandom (not attacker-controlled, but determines which slot is freed)\",\"operation\":\"FREE msg[index] then swap-remove without nulling freed pointer\",\"risk\":\"HIGH\",\"reason\":\"After free(msg[index]), if index == cookie_num-1, the swap writes the same freed pointer back into msg[index], leaving a dangling pointer. Even if index != cookie_num-1, the freed chunk may be reallocated by subsequent create_cookie or strdup, and the old pointer in msg[cookie_num-1] (now moved to msg[index]) still points to valid memory — but the freed chunk itself can be reused. The freed pointer is never nulled, creating potential UAF if the freed chunk is reallocated and then accessed via edit/read.\"},{\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"input\":\"index via scanf(%llu) and edit_data via read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1)\",\"operation\":\"WRITE into msg[index] buffer with size = msg_size[index] - 1\",\"risk\":\"HIGH\",\"reason\":\"The read size is computed as msg_size[index] (int32) - 1, then sign-extended via movsxd. If msg_size[index] == 0, the result is -1 → 0xFFFFFFFF (sign-extended to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF), causing read() to attempt writing a massive amount into the heap buffer. This is a potential heap overflow. Additionally, if msg[index] points to freed memory (UAF from eat_cookie), this write goes into a freed chunk.\"},{\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"input\":\"index via scanf(%llu)\",\"operation\":\"READ msg[index] and print via printf(%s)\",\"risk\":\"HIGH\",\"reason\":\"If msg[index] points to freed/reallocated heap memory (UAF from eat_cookie), printf(%s) will print whatever is in that memory, potentially leaking heap metadata or other data. This is a potential info leak.\"},{\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"input\":\"index via scanf(%llu)\",\"operation\":\"index check uses signed jl but index is read as unsigned %llu\",\"risk\":\"MEDIUM\",\"reason\":\"The index is read via scanf(%llu) (unsigned) but the bounds check uses 'cmp rdx,rax; jl' (signed less-than). If cookie_num is small and index is a large unsigned value with bit 63 set, the signed comparison may pass, allowing OOB access to msg[] and msg_size[] arrays. However, this requires cookie_num to be positive and the index to have bit 63 set, which is an edge case.\"},{\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"input\":\"index via scanf(%llu)\",\"operation\":\"same signed/unsigned mismatch in bounds check\",\"risk\":\"MEDIUM\",\"reason\":\"Same signed jl comparison on unsigned %llu input as edit_cookie — potential OOB read of msg[] array.\"},{\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"input\":\"size via scanf(%lld)\",\"operation\":\"calloc(size, 1) then read(0, buf, size)\",\"risk\":\"LOW\",\"reason\":\"Size is checked <= 0x100 and calloc zeroes memory. The read size equals the allocation size, so no overflow here. The size is stored as int32 in msg_size[].\"}],\"facts\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Binary is a 64-bit PIE ELF, dynamically linked, not stripped, compiled with GCC 10.2.0\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F002\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Security: Full RELRO, NX enabled, Canary, PIE enabled, no FORTIFY\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F003\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"libc is Ubuntu GLIBC 2.39-0ubuntu8.8 at /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6\",\"source\":\"RUNTIME\"},{\"id\":\"F004\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"BSS layout: msg (0x4060, 32×8=256 bytes, char* array), msg_size (0x4160, 32×4=128 bytes, int32 array), urandom (0x41e0, 8 bytes, FILE*), cookie_num (0x41e8, 8 bytes, int64). msg and msg_size are parallel arrays indexed by the same cookie index.\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F005\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"init() pre-creates 5 fortune cookies via strdup into msg[0..4] with sizes 0x50,0x30,0x18,0x38,0x40 in msg_size[0..4], sets cookie_num=5\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F006\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"create_cookie: scanf(%lld) for size, checks size<=0x100, calloc(size,1), read(0,buf,size), stores in msg[cookie_num] and msg_size[cookie_num], cookie_num++. Check cookie_num<=0x1f (max 32 slots).\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F007\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie: reads 1 random byte from /dev/urandom, index=byte%cookie_num, prints msg[index] via printf(%s), frees msg[index], swap-removes msg[cookie_num-1]→msg[index] and msg_size[cookie_num-1]→msg_size[index], cookie_num--. Freed pointer is NOT nulled.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F008\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie: scanf(%llu) for index, checks index<cookie_num via signed jl, reads msg_size[index]-1 bytes into msg[index] via read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1). Size computed as int32-1 then sign-extended via movsxd.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F009\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"read_cookie: scanf(%llu) for index, checks index<cookie_num via signed jl, prints msg[index] via printf(%s).\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F010\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"In eat_cookie, when index == cookie_num-1 (the last element), the swap-remove writes msg[cookie_num-1] back into msg[index] (same slot), so msg[index] still contains the freed pointer — a dangling pointer remains in the msg[] array.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F011\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"In edit_cookie, if msg_size[index] == 0, the expression msg_size[index]-1 yields -1 (int32), which is sign-extended via movsxd to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, causing read() to attempt writing ~4 exabytes into the heap buffer at msg[index].\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F012\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie and read_cookie both use scanf(%llu) for index but check bounds with 'cmp rdx,rax; jl' (signed less-than). If index has bit 63 set, the signed comparison treats it as negative, potentially passing the check and allowing OOB array access.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F013\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"GOT is read-only (Full RELRO) — GOT overwrite is not viable. All GOT entries are in the RELRO-protected region.\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F014\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"alarm(60) is set in init(), limiting runtime to 60 seconds.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F015\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"The index in eat_cookie is determined by a random byte from /dev/urandom modulo cookie_num — the attacker does NOT directly control which cookie is freed.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F016\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg_size entries are stored as int32 (DWORD) but cookie_num and msg entries are int64/pointer (QWORD). create_cookie stores size via 'mov ecx,edx' (truncates to 32-bit) into msg_size[].\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F017\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"The 5 initial strdup allocations in init() create heap chunks of sizes 0x50, 0x30, 0x18, 0x38, 0x40 (plus strdup overhead). These are in the same heap arena as subsequent create_cookie calloc calls.\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F018\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"description\":\"msg array (0x4060, 256 bytes) and msg_size array (0x4160, 128 bytes) are contiguous in BSS with no gap between them (0x4060+256=0x4160). urandom (0x41e0) follows msg_size (0x4160+128=0x41e0). cookie_num (0x41e8) follows urandom.\",\"source\":\"ELF\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"id\":\"U001\",\"description\":\"Whether the signed/unsigned mismatch in edit_cookie/read_cookie bounds check is practically exploitable — requires index with bit 63 set via scanf(%llu), and the behavior of jl on such values needs runtime verification.\",\"reason\":\"Static analysis shows the mismatch, but actual exploitability depends on runtime behavior of scanf(%llu) with large values and the signed comparison.\"},{\"id\":\"U002\",\"description\":\"Whether msg_size[index] can be set to 0 by an attacker — create_cookie stores the user-provided size (which must be >0 for calloc to return non-NULL), but the swap-remove in eat_cookie could potentially leave a slot with msg_size=0 if the last element's size is 0. Need to verify if any code path can produce msg_size[i]=0.\",\"reason\":\"The init() pre-set sizes are all non-zero. create_cookie checks size<=0x100 but does not check size>0. If size=0, calloc(0,1) may return NULL or a minimal allocation, and msg_size would be 0.\"},{\"id\":\"U003\",\"description\":\"Whether the eat_cookie UAF (dangling pointer when index==cookie_num-1) can be reliably triggered — the index is random (byte % cookie_num), so the attacker cannot directly control which slot is freed.\",\"reason\":\"The randomness comes from /dev/urandom, which is not predictable. However, by manipulating cookie_num (creating/deleting cookies), the attacker can influence the modulo result.\"},{\"id\":\"U004\",\"description\":\"CET (IBT/SHSTK) status is unknown — checksec does not report it and the ELF may or may not have CET-related notes.\",\"reason\":\"No CET information available from standard tools.\"},{\"id\":\"U005\",\"description\":\"Whether calloc(0, 1) in create_cookie returns NULL or a valid minimal allocation on glibc 2.39 — if it returns NULL, msg[cookie_num] would be NULL and subsequent edit/read would crash.\",\"reason\":\"Implementation-defined behavior of calloc(0,1) needs runtime verification.\"}],\"raw\":{\"elf\":\"ELF64 LSB pie executable, x86-64, dynamically linked, interpreter /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2, not stripped, BuildID=84dab319bf6fe22134cf0338cbd8071fd8bc06c2, for GNU/Linux 3.2.0, GCC 10.2.0 (Debian)\",\"sections\":\"29 sections. Key: .text@0x1110(0x891,AX), .rodata@0x2000(0x266,A), .data@0x4000(0x10,WA), .bss@0x4020(0x1d0,WA), .got@0x3f58(0xa8,WA→RELRO), .plt@0x1020(0xe0,AX), .init_array@0x3d58(0x8,WA→RELRO), .fini_array@0x3d60(0x8,WA→RELRO), .dynamic@0x3d68(0x1f0,WA→RELRO)\",\"symbols\":\"Key user functions: _abort@0x11f5, init@0x1232, create_cookie@0x1399, eat_cookie@0x14e1, edit_cookie@0x1628, read_cookie@0x1751, menu@0x17fd, main@0x187f. Key globals: msg@0x4060(256B,char*[32]), msg_size@0x4160(128B,int32[32]), urandom@0x41e0(8B,FILE*), cookie_num@0x41e8(8B,int64)\",\"disassembly\":\"Full disassembly of all 8 user functions obtained. Key data flows: eat_cookie frees without nulling (UAF), edit_cookie uses msg_size[idx]-1 as read size (potential integer underflow to 0xFFFFFFFF when msg_size=0), read_cookie prints msg[idx] as string (potential info leak), edit/read_cookie use signed jl on unsigned %llu index (potential OOB).\"}},\"vulnerability_report\":null,\"primitive_reports\":[],\"target_bug\":\"\",\"bug_reports\":[],\"impact_reports\":[],\"strategy_reports\":[],\"final_exploit_path\":\"\",\"final_report\":{}}",
